// The port of connect() must be an integer, and an integer is an Int or an
// integer-valued Number (spec/05-stdlib.md, Integer arguments). A program that
// computed a port writes int(l.port()), so the Int form is the natural one. A
// fractional port is a runtime error that halts the program, and the check
// comes before any connection attempt.
// COVERS: integer-arg connect-port
// STATUS: error
// TIMEOUT: 10
// CHECK: connected
var l = listen("127.0.0.1", 0);
var c = connect("127.0.0.1", int(l.port()));
print "connected";
connect("127.0.0.1", 1.5);
print "unreachable";
